     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">Hi, <div><br></div><div>With the output you get, you can plot the tree using the plot.phylo function in ape (<a href=\"https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/ape/versions/4.1/topics/plot.phylo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/ape/versions/4.1/topics/plot.phylo&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792480694901000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2d8PGpLcxwPJ7JnBm6Gmx7\">https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/ape/versions/4.1/topics/plot.phylo</a>)</div><div><br></div><div>There are a lot of parameters, so you will need to play around with them to get an optimal solution. Otherwise, you may need to increase your canvas size: <a href=\"https://stackoverflow.com/a/7405548/2752888\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://stackoverflow.com/a/7405548/2752888&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792480694901000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3NZywV1keKffORm-p1LP27\">https://stackoverflow.com/a/7405548/2752888</a></div><div><br></div><div>There is also the ggtree package on Bioconductor: <a href=\"https://guangchuangyu.github.io/ggtree/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://guangchuangyu.github.io/ggtree/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792480694901000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0dQd5BA1PfpnNVa0bPlCli\">https://guangchuangyu.github.io/ggtree/</a></div><div><br></div><div>Sorry I&#39;m not able to give you one perfect solution. I hope these can help get you started.</div><div><br></div><div>Zhian</div><div><br></div><div><div>\r\n<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">-----</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">Zhian N. Kamvar, Ph. D.</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">Postdoctoral Researcher (Everhart Lab)</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">Department of Plant Pathology</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">University of Nebraska-Lincoln</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">ORCID: 0000-0003-1458-7108</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><br></div><br></div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<br><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On Sep 29, 2017, at 05:19 , genetist &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">blackt...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>hi to all</div><div><br></div><div>I used aboot function in Poppr package for boot strap analysis of my tree and I used show tree option as TURE. I got tree plotted but in that genotypes were so crowded and unable to interpret them very well. is there any option to make this this more readbale? please help me in this regard and any help would be highly appreciated</div><div>thanks in advance</div></div><div><br></div>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;poppr&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">poppr+un...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo post to this group, send email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">po...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/poppr/901787b5-2194-4f41-b43c-1dc4d927594c%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/poppr/901787b5-2194-4f41-b43c-1dc4d927594c%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792480694901000&amp;usg=AOvVaw254PO260dsDseyPfF02jav\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/poppr/901787b5-2194-4f41-b43c-1dc4d927594c%40googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792480694901000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0s_pkq72hkJKO0ixWUtrXu\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n<span>&lt;boot.jpeg&gt;</span></div></blockquote></div><br></div></div>"
